<title>LEBANON: Solidere shares fall in Beirut.</title>
<headline>Solidere shares fall in Beirut.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Solidere shares fell on the Beirut Stock Exchange on Tuesday as A shares closed at $110 from Monday's $110.125 and B shares dropped to $114 from $115.</p>
<p>Turnover in Solidere shares was 7,831 shares from 6,862 on Monday and value was $872,134 from $764,860.</p>
<p>Piping maker Eternit held steady at $1.75 with 3,000 shares changing hands. A block of 70,000 Ciments Libanais shares were traded over the counter at $1.20. They traded at $1.18 on the BSE a day earlier.</p>
<p>The LISPI stock index fell 0.14 percent to 81.77 and the BLOM stock index also fell 0.42 percent to 941.77.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (9611) 353078 645456 602057</p>
